Z||000000||L.I. Fieros||04-11-2001||12:59 AM||||The Long Island Fiero Enthusiasts Navigational Road Rally is coming and you're all invited!  The event is being held in the Huntington area out on Long Island on May 12th.  This is a driving event, not a show.  There of course will be plenty of time to hang out by the cars after the rally during lunch though.  Speaking of which, lunch is included in your registration fee and will be waiting for you at the finish line.  Registration is $5 for each car and $5 for each participant.  Pre-registration (prior to May 1st.) is very important for planning and lunch.  We appreciate your help on this.  The exact amount of time that the rally will take has not been finalized yet, but it will be challenging and lots of fun.  So, beware of who you follow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> We may also have a Fiero cruise following lunch.  Registration is from 9-10am and the first car will be sent off at 10am.  If you have any questions or would like directions to the "starting line" please e-mail me at defannin@suffolk.lib.ny.us<P>Please Note: In the interest of safety, everyone who wishes to compete will be required to have a navigator assisting them.  On the morning of the event we will do our best to combine those who are singles into groups of two.<P>Are you up to the challenge?<P>See ya,<BR>Dave<BR>-- No time to learn how to post a sig. yet. --||||reg||1
